55 SSET2~
When using 'sset <sn> affect stripsn' you can now use the spell name instead
of using the spell's sn.
ex: sset 433 affect stripsn 'blindness'

To apply an affect to caster only or caster and victim, place an excaimation
mark before the affect to be placed on the caster.
ex: sset 433 affect !strength 5 l*5
This will add +5 strength to the caster for level*5 rnds and any additional
affects will be applied to the spell's target.

Another affect that can be added is the 'jump' affect. This affect will cause
the caster to be removed from combat.
ex: sset 455 affect jump

To create a stun effect use the 'wait' affect. Supply a number in a multiple
of 10 per each second of stun you want to apply.
For instance, to apply 5 seconds of stun you would use:
sset 455 affect wait 0 50
~
