1 VERBAL NON-VERBAL NONVERBAL~
There are two different types of spells when it comes to casting them. There
are verbal and non-verbal types. The verbal types must be uttered when cast.
If the caster cannot utter the spell, then it cannot be cast. Non-verbal
spells, on the other hand, can be cast without uttering a word. This is
usually done by memorizing a series of hand movements. The non-verbal spell
may also be cast with the simple use of the caster's breath.
~
