1 'CONJURERS EQUIPMENT'~
&WIf the conjurer is the victim of a &RPK&W, all the conjurer enchanted items
will start to rot. If they are &RNOT&W held in the &Yimmediate inventory &w
(ie: if you type 'inventory' and do not see the items, they are not in your
immediate inventory)&W of a player within &R5&W minutes, the enchanted items
will totally decay and be destroyed. If the items are being held in a player's
inventory, they become owned by that player. The conjurer-only flag fades away
and the items become inventory. This means that upon the next death of that
player &w(death by mob or by PK)&W, the items are destroyed.

This has no effect if the conjurer was killed by a mob.&D
~
60 OGET~
Syntax: oget <id>
        oget v<vnum>

Oget will retrieve any item in the realm using its id number or vnum. If the
vnum is used, it will retrieve the first item it comes across that matches the
specified vnum. Using the id number is more precise and will retrieve the
exact object requested.
~
1 'PIERCE SHADOWS'~
Syntax: cast 'pierce shadows'

The caster of this spell summons forth a powerful glowing blade that will
slice through anyone or anything trying to be unseen in the room, leaving them
damaged and stunned.
~
1 SALT WOUNDS 'SALT WOUNDS'~
~
1 EQSWAPPING 'EQUIPMENT SWAPPING'~
At no time can a player transfer gold or equipment of ANY sort (this includes,
but is not limited to, quest, stock, and randoms) to any character played by
or owned by the "donator". This further includes an immortal facilitated
destroy. Even a character of the same name and same history is still a
different entity and therefore cannot profit or retain anything from the
previous incarnation. Special consideration will be given to extenuating
circumstances and can only be authorized by an Implementor.
~
1 'ENHANCE TREASURE'~
Syntax: cast 'enhance treasure' <object>

Items of type 'treasure' or 'arttreasure' may be enhanced with this spell,
yielding an addition to spell damage and mana points. This spell can enhance
magical as well as non-magical items but may not be used to enhance an item
that is already enchanted.
~
1 'ENHANCE ARMOR'~
Syntax: cast 'enhance armor' <object>

Items of type 'armor' or 'artarmor' may be enhanced with this spell,
yielding an addition to mana points, armor class and svs. This spell can
enchant magical as well as non-magical items but may not be used to enhance
an item that is already enchanted. However, if the item is magical the
enhancement will not be as powerful as it could be otherwise. This spell also
causes the item to be aligned with the alignment with the caster.
~
1 'ENHANCE WEAPON'~
Syntax: cast 'enhance weapon' <object>

Items of type 'weapon' or 'artweapon' may be enhanced with this spell,
yielding an addition to spell damage. This spell can enhance magical as
well as non-magical weapons but may not be used to enhance a weapon that
is already enchanted. However, if the weapon is magical the enhancement
will not be as powerful as it could be otherwise. This spell also causes
the weapon to be aligned with the alignment with the caster.
~
1 ABBAFFS~
&WWith this setting turned on (config +abbaffs) you will see a combined
abbreviated affects list. For example, if normally you would see this:
&P(&WSanct&P) (&RFS&P) (&BSS&P) (&CIS&P) (&CInvis&P) (&BHide&P) (&WTranslucent&P)&W
With ABBAFFS on, you would see this:
&P( &WS &RF &BK &CI &WV &BH &YT &P)&W

Letter abbreviations:
  &WS&W - Sanctuary
  &RF&W - Fireshield
  &BK&W - Shockshield
  &CI&W - Iceshield
  &WV&W - Invis/Improved invis/Mass invis
  &BH&W - Hide
  &GC&W - Camo
  &YT&W - Pass door (Translucent)
  &PP&W - Faerie fire/Faerie fog (Pink aura)
~
1 CONVERT~
Syntax: convert
        convert <class>

&WThis command allows a &Ctiered&W character to set their dualclass to a new
class by allowing you to choose a class from your available pre-tier classes.
(If you are an archmagi, you may choose to 'convert mage' 'convert druid' or
'convert conjurer' etc.)

If your 'whois' lists you as only &CArchmagi&W, &CBishop&W, &CChampion&W or
&CRogue&W you will need to use this command and choose a class. If you do not
choose a class, you will see a message asking you to choose one.

For &Cnon-tiered&D characters, this command will remove any skills that have
been removed from your class(es) or skills that you have obtained through
other means.&D
~
1 VERSION VERSIONS 'VERSION NOTE' 'VERSION NOTES'~
The following is a list of versions that you can get information on regarding
the changes made in that version.

